# Backend Rules (`server/`)

Spec: `docs/platform/01_BACKEND_SPECIFICATION.md`, standards: `docs/platform/10_CODING_STANDARDS_AND_CONVENTIONS.md`.

## Module layout (mandatory)
`src/modules/<module>/<module>.{router,controller,service,repository,schemas,policies,events,mapper}.ts` + `__tests__/`.
- Controllers: parse → call service → return envelope. No Prisma, no business logic.
- Services: business rules (doc 06), one transaction per use case, call engines (`src/engines/*`).
- Repositories: Prisma only, explicit `select`, apply `ScopeFilter`, return `null`/arrays (never throw `AppError`).

## Request pipeline
`authenticate` → `authorize('module:action')` → `validate({params, query, body})` (zod) → controller.
Every route declares a permission key from doc 03 Appendix A. Never skip `authorize` on a mutating route.

## Responses & errors
- Success: `{ data, meta? }`. Errors: throw `AppError` subclasses from `src/core/errors.ts`; never `res.status(500).json(...)` by hand.
- Invalid lifecycle moves throw `InvalidStateTransitionError(from, to)` (409).
- Money: `Prisma.Decimal` in, string out via mapper. Dates: UTC ISO out; `Asia/Dhaka` only for business-day math.

## Data
- Soft delete via Prisma extension; never hard-delete audited models.
- Reference numbers only via `sequence.next('PREFIX')` inside the creating transaction.
- New list query on a large table → add index in migration and attach `EXPLAIN ANALYZE` to the PR.
- Migrations: expand → backfill → contract. No destructive migration without approval.

## Async & realtime
- Anything > 300 ms (PDF, AV scan, exports, roll-ups, fan-out to many users) goes to a BullMQ job with a deterministic `jobId`; processors must be idempotent.
- Emit Socket.IO events through `src/core/realtime` helpers after the DB transaction commits, never inside it.

## Logging & security
- `logger.child({ module })`; never log tokens, passwords, OTPs, NID, raw request bodies.
- Validate every input with zod; no raw SQL string interpolation (`$queryRaw` tagged template only).

## Tests
- Each endpoint: happy path + authz denial + validation failure (Vitest + Supertest + Testcontainers).
- Services with rules from doc 06: unit tests referencing the `BR-xx-nn` id in the test name.
